---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-virtual-list</code> shows a long list, such as 10,000 people, by rendering only the
  items in view plus <code>overscan</code> items on each side. Set <code>items</code> to the array
  and <code>renderItem</code> to a function that renders one item. Every item is
  <code>item-height</code> pixels high (48 by default). The list scrolls inside itself, so give it a
  height; the default is <code>20rem</code>.
</p>
<p>
  Items are rendered into the list's own light DOM, each inside a
  <code>&lt;div role="listitem"&gt;</code>, so your page styles apply to them. The list manages
  its children: do not add your own.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-virtual-list
    id='virtual-list-demo'
    label='People'
    item-height='48'
    style='width: 100%; max-width: 360px; height: 20rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant);'
  ></wc-virtual-list>
  <script is:inline>
    const $list = document.getElementById('virtual-list-demo');
    $list.items = Array.from({ length: 10000 }, (_, index) => ({
      name: `Person ${index + 1}`,
      email: `person${index + 1}@example.com`,
    }));
    // Plain JavaScript: return a DOM node (or a string).
    $list.renderItem = (person, index) => {
      const row = document.createElement('div');
      row.style.cssText = 'display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;height:100%;padding:0 1rem;';
      row.innerHTML = '<strong></strong><small></small>';
      row.querySelector('strong').textContent = person.name;
      row.querySelector('small').textContent = person.email;
      return row;
    };
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Rendering with Lit</h3>
<p>
  In a Lit component, return a template. Use arrow functions for event listeners inside it, since
  the list, not your component, renders the template.
</p>

<pre><code>{`import { html } from 'lit';

html\`<wc-virtual-list
  label="People"
  item-height="48"
  .items=\${this.people}
  .renderItem=\${(person, index) => html\`<div class="row" @click=\${() => this.open(person)}>
    \${index + 1}. \${person.name}
  </div>\`}
></wc-virtual-list>\`;`}</code></pre>

<h3>Scrolling to an item</h3>
<p>
  <code>scrollToIndex(index, {'{'} align, behavior {'}'})</code> scrolls an item into view.
  <code>align</code> is <code>start</code>, <code>center</code>, <code>end</code> or
  <code>nearest</code> (the default, which scrolls only as far as needed). <code>behavior:
  'smooth'</code> animates, unless the person prefers reduced motion.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; width: 100%; max-width: 360px;'>
    <wc-button id='virtual-list-jump'>Go to item 5,000</wc-button>
    <wc-virtual-list
      id='virtual-list-scroll'
      label='Numbers'
      item-height='32'
      style='height: 12rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant);'
    ></wc-virtual-list>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    const $numbers = document.getElementById('virtual-list-scroll');
    $numbers.items = Array.from({ length: 10000 }, (_, index) => `Item ${index + 1}`);
    $numbers.renderItem = item => item;
    document.getElementById('virtual-list-jump').addEventListener('click', () => {
      $numbers.scrollToIndex(4999, { align: 'center', behavior: 'smooth' });
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
